    {
      "pattern": "^git(?!.*\\s--output\\b)(?:\\s+(?:-C\\s+[^\\s-]\\S*|--no-pager|--paginate|-p|--no-replace-objects|--literal-pathspecs|--no-optional-locks))*\\s+(?:status|log|diff|show|describe|rev-parse|ls-files|ls-tree|shortlog|blame|annotate|cherry|whatchanged|ls-remote)\\b",
      "comment": "Git read-only subcommands. The pre-subcommand flags are ENUMERATED, not `-[A-Za-z]`: `git -c core.pager=<cmd>` and `--config-env` inject config that executes, so only the navigation/pager flags are accepted. `--output` is refused because `git diff --output=FILE` writes it."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "^git(?:\\s+(?:-C\\s+[^\\s-]\\S*|--no-pager|--paginate|-p|--no-replace-objects|--literal-pathspecs|--no-optional-locks))*\\s+stash\\s+list\\b",
      "comment": "Git stash listing (read-only)"
    },
    {
      "pattern": "^git(?:\\s+(?:-C\\s+[^\\s-]\\S*|--no-pager|--paginate|-p|--no-replace-objects|--literal-pathspecs|--no-optional-locks))*\\s+config\\s+(?:--get|--get-all|--get-regexp|--list|-l)\\b",
      "comment": "Git config READ forms only"
    },
    {
      "pattern": "^git(?:\\s+(?:-C\\s+[^\\s-]\\S*|--no-pager|--paginate|-p|--no-replace-objects|--literal-pathspecs|--no-optional-locks))*\\s+branch(?:\\s+(?:--list|--all|--remotes|--verbose|-[arvli]+|--show-current|--merged|--no-merged|--contains|--no-contains|--points-at|--ignore-case|-i|--column|--no-column|--color|--no-color|--abbrev|--no-abbrev|(?:--sort|--format|--color|--abbrev)=\\S*))*$",
      "comment": "Git branch LISTING only: the flag set is enumerated and the pattern is end-anchored, so `-d/-D/-m/-M/-c/-C/-f/-u` and a bare NAME operand (which CREATES a branch) are refused. `-a` is a listing flag HERE and is deliberately absent from the tag entry, where it means --annotate (P2.112)."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "^git(?:\\s+(?:-C\\s+[^\\s-]\\S*|--no-pager|--paginate|-p|--no-replace-objects|--literal-pathspecs|--no-optional-locks))*\\s+tag(?:\\s+(?:--list|-[lin]+|-n[0-9]*|--merged|--no-merged|--contains|--no-contains|--points-at|--ignore-case|-i|--color|--no-color|--omit-empty|(?:--sort|--format|--color)=\\S*))*$",
      "comment": "Git tag LISTING only: end-anchored with an enumerated flag set, so `-a/-s/-d/-f/-m` and a bare NAME operand (which CREATES a tag) are refused. `-a` is NOT accepted here even though the branch entry accepts it: same letter, opposite action (P2.112)."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "^git(?:\\s+(?:-C\\s+[^\\s-]\\S*|--no-pager|--paginate|-p|--no-replace-objects|--literal-pathspecs|--no-optional-locks))*\\s+remote(?:\\s+(?:-v|--verbose))*$",
      "comment": "Git remote listing (bare/-v only; `add`/`remove`/`set-url` write .git/config)"
    },
    {
      "pattern": "^git(?:\\s+(?:-C\\s+[^\\s-]\\S*|--no-pager|--paginate|-p|--no-replace-objects|--literal-pathspecs|--no-optional-locks))*\\s+remote(?:\\s+(?:-v|--verbose))*\\s+(?:show|get-url)(?:\\s+(?:-n|--push|--all|[^\\s-]\\S*))*$",
      "comment": "Git remote READ verbs: show, get-url"
    },
    {
      "pattern": "^git(?:\\s+(?:-C\\s+[^\\s-]\\S*|--no-pager|--paginate|-p|--no-replace-objects|--literal-pathspecs|--no-optional-locks))*\\s+reflog(?:\\s+show)?(?:\\s+(?:-[0-9]+|--all|--no-abbrev|--abbrev(?:=\\S*)?|--date=\\S+|--oneline|--pretty(?:=\\S*)?))*$",
      "comment": "Git reflog READ only: end-anchored, so `expire`/`delete`/`drop` — which destroy reflog entries — are refused. `git history` is NOT accepted at all: it is not a git builtin, so it dispatches to a user ALIAS, and a git alias may be `!<shell command>`."
    },
    {
      "pattern": "^gh\\s+(pr|issue|repo|release|run|workflow|gist|project)\\s+(view|list|status|diff|checks|comments)\\b",
      "comment": "GitHub CLI read operations: view PRs, issues, releases"
    },
    {
      "pattern": "^gh\\s+api\\b(?!.*\\s-[XfF](?:[\\s=]|$))(?!.*\\s--(?:field|raw-field|input)(?:[\\s=]|$))(?!.*\\s--method(?:[\\s=])(?!GET\\b))",
      "comment": "GitHub API, GET only. Replaces the earlier `--method GET` / no-`--method` pair, which both read only the LONG flag: `-X` is gh's short form of `--method`, and `-f`/`-F`/`--field`/`--raw-field`/`--input` make gh switch to POST with no method flag at all. All of those are refused here, and `--method` is accepted only with the value GET. Restored in bundle 2026-10-09.2 (UA12.184): upstream v0.14.0's two entries, shipped in 2026-10-09, re-opened gh api writes and uploads on the PowerShell route, which reads a smart-quoted span as ONE word where bash splits it."
    },
    {
